Missing standard COMMON-LISP symbols — residual list after the v1.8.57 audit.

A kind-aware audit of all 978 CL external symbols (fboundp /
macro-function / special-operator-p / boundp / find-class / lambda-list
keywords / declarations / type-only names) ran at v1.8.57.  33 genuine
gaps were implemented then: *MACROEXPAND-HOOK* (honored by
MACROEXPAND-1) and *BREAK-ON-SIGNALS* (variable; kernel signalling does
not consult it yet), METHOD-QUALIFIERS, FUNCTION-KEYWORDS,
COMPUTE-APPLICABLE-METHODS, ADD-METHOD, REMOVE-METHOD,
ALLOCATE-INSTANCE, NO-APPLICABLE-METHOD, NO-NEXT-METHOD (both wired
into %GF-DISPATCH / %CNM-CALL), SLOT-MISSING, SLOT-UNBOUND (wired into
SLOT-VALUE), INVALID-METHOD-ERROR, METHOD-COMBINATION-ERROR,
MAKE-INSTANCES-OBSOLETE, UPDATE-INSTANCE-FOR-REDEFINED-CLASS,
COPY-STRUCTURE, PACKAGE-ERROR-PACKAGE, FILE-POSITION (new C builtin:
ftell/fseek with :START/:END), FILE-STRING-LENGTH, FORMATTER, STEP,
INSPECT, TRACE, UNTRACE (real call tracing with depth on
*TRACE-OUTPUT*), and the degraded-but-functional pretty-printer entry
points PPRINT-DISPATCH, PPRINT-FILL, PPRINT-LINEAR, PPRINT-TABULAR,
PPRINT-TAB, PPRINT-LOGICAL-BLOCK, PPRINT-POP,
PPRINT-EXIT-IF-LIST-EXHAUSTED (no layout engine: linear output).
FILE-LENGTH (the original report) was already implemented.

REMAINING (5 — composite streams DONE v1.8.61), by dependency:

1. Composite-stream accessors (6): ECHO-STREAM-INPUT-STREAM,
   ECHO-STREAM-OUTPUT-STREAM, TWO-WAY-STREAM-INPUT-STREAM,
   TWO-WAY-STREAM-OUTPUT-STREAM, CONCATENATED-STREAM-STREAMS,
   SYNONYM-STREAM-SYMBOL.
   DONE (v1.8.61): the four MAKE-* constructors now build real composite
   stream objects, and all six accessors + the four *-STREAM-P predicates
   are implemented.  Design: each composite is a genuine FILE-STREAM backed
   by a cookie FILE* (fopencookie/funopen) whose read/write callbacks
   forward, IN PURE C, to the component streams — resolving their FILE*s and
   doing fgetc/fputc with no allocation, no evaluator re-entry, so they are
   GC-safe inside the kernel reader (unlike the Lisp-callback OUTPUT stream).
   Concatenated advances past exhausted components (feof); echo tees each
   read char to the output side; synonym re-resolves SYMBOL-VALUE per op;
   two-way splits input/output.  A new kernel primitive
   BOCL::%MAKE-COMPOSITE-STREAM (callback_stream.c) + a composite_kind field
   on FileStream back it; the CL registry drives predicates/accessors.
   Because everything routes through stream_cstream()'s FILE*, READ /
   READ-CHAR / PEEK-CHAR / WRITE-CHAR / LISTEN all work uniformly, including
   full (READ composite-stream) parses.  Covered by the "composite streams"
   case in tests/test_conformance.c.
   Note: the *-STREAM-P predicates (STRING-STREAM-P, FILE-STREAM-P,
   TWO-WAY-STREAM-P, ...) are bocl EXTENSIONS, not standard CL, so — like
   the pre-existing BROADCAST-STREAM-P — they are interned in COMMON-LISP as
   INTERNAL symbols (accessible as CL::TWO-WAY-STREAM-P, not as a bare name
   from CL-USER).  The six accessors ARE standard CL and are exported.

2. Special forms without MACRO-FUNCTION visibility (5): DEFMACRO,
   HANDLER-CASE, HANDLER-BIND, RESTART-BIND, RESTART-CASE are
   implemented as evaluator special forms (fully functional), but
   MACRO-FUNCTION returns NIL for them and they are not in
   SPECIAL-OPERATOR-P's ANSI list.  Conformance-visibility only;
   becomes real macro definitions in the def-forms Phase-2 plan
   (see bocl-defun-lexical-block notes).

The audit script is now committed as
issues/open/audit-cl-symbols.lisp (run with
  sources/bocl -n -Q -b --on-error exit -l issues/open/audit-cl-symbols.lisp -q
from the repo root); re-run it after any of the above to keep this
list honest.  Re-run 2026-07-19 at v1.9.0 for the CL-STATUS refresh:
both residual groups confirmed unchanged; the marker/type-specifier
probes it prompted are filed as type-specifier-conformance.issue.
